     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7712\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to designating\nas peace officers dog control officers of the village of Holley\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to provide dog control officers in\nthe village of Holley with peace officer status.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1 of this bill amends § 2.10 of the Criminal Procedure Law by\nadding a new subdivision 88 to provide peace officer status to  the  dog\ncontrol officers in the village of Holley.\n\nThis  will  allow the village board to designate the dog control officer\nas a constable for purposes of enforcement of Article 26 of the Agricul-\nture and Markets Law, and for the purpose of issuing appearance  tickets\nunder Article 7 of the Agriculture and Markets Law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was introduced at the request of the village of Holley.\nThe  village  deems it important that its dog control officer have peace\nofficer status. The abilities that accompany peace officer status  iden-\ntified  in  Criminal  Procedure Law § 2.20, will better help dog control\nofficers to recognize and investigate circumstances of abuse and cruelty\ntowards animals.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
